<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuanku Syed Sirajuddin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sirajuddin of Perlis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tuanku Syed Sirajuddin is the Raja of Perlis, a Malaysian state ruled by the Jamalullail family, who succeeded his father Tuanku Syed Putra in 2000. Under Malaysia's system of rotating monarchy he was elected by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-rulers">Conference of Rulers</a> and served as the twelfth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</a>, the country's king, from 2001 to 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuanku-syed-sirajuddin.jpg" alt="Tuanku Syed Sirajuddin" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Embassy Kuala Lumpur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sirajuddin_of_Perlis_in_2018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
